31,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I found out that only two firms are tendering for the big digging work, and they are worried about clay and slippage. Also, the southern part is easier to fence off than the center.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,May,,"My findings are a bit sobering. The cost to maintain planted and water-managed areas is triple that of hard surfaces, and that gap is only getting wider every year. It's a pricey habit!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It is a bit sad to see, but my research shows that many of our young trees didn't survive their second summer because watering was forgotten. Some older works hold up well, but others need constant patching.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The groundskeeping roll has shrunk significantly, leaving only seven posts. While we have some casual support and two dedicated volunteer groups, the core staffing for daily maintenance is quite thin.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"The ground is fighting us. People are carving their own paths to the tram, and the drainage is failing since the culvert was capped. It's a heat trap that doesn't drain.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, that sounds scary that the ground is fighting us. If the drainage is failing and the firms are worried about clay and slippage, maybe we should be careful about where we dig?","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,May,,"@Victoria, with only seven posts left, we're in trouble if we pick a plan that's high-maintenance. We can't afford to be fancy if we can't actually pay for the upkeep.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@May, you are quite right to be cautious. It would be a shame to create something beautiful only to watch it fade because we didn't plan for the care it needs.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@May, I agree. The reliance on a shrinking core staff is a major risk. If we choose a design that requires constant, specialized attention, it will likely suffer the same fate as the trees Shizue mentioned.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""May"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Minato, it's not scary, just reality. If we ignore the tram-commuter shortcuts and the drainage failures, we're just designing a pretty picture that will be a swampy mess in three years.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Minato,,"I see. I hope we can find a way to make it work. @Shunichi, if the center is a swampy mess, does that mean the southern part is safer since it's easier to fence off?","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,May,,"@Minato, fencing is one thing, but the real nightmare is the budget. If we build something that requires expensive specialist care, we'll be bankrupt before the first anniversary. We need something low-maintenance.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Victoria, it is heartening that we have volunteers, but we must be gentle with them. We cannot expect our dear community members to make up for a lack of professional care and planning.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Shizue, I agree. Volunteers are a wonderful asset, but they cannot replace a professional rota. We must ensure the plan is manageable for the seven remaining staff members without overextending our community support.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, your budget anxiety is noted, but let's be rational. Low-maintenance doesn't mean ""cheap."" It means designing for the actual flow of people and the reality of the soil, not a fantasy.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Minato,,"I think we should all be very careful. If the soil is slippery and the drainage is bad, maybe we should pick a plan that doesn't need too much big digging in the center.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,May,,"Exactly, Minato. Let's keep it simple. If we avoid the ""fancy"" water features and excessive planting, we save the budget and the staff's sanity. I'm voting for the path of least resistance and lowest cost.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"I agree with May. Let us look for a plan that is honest about its needs. It would be much kinder to the city to have a modest, lasting park than a grand one that withers.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Victoria,,I concur. We must prioritize operational viability over aesthetic ambition. A plan that aligns with our current staffing levels and avoids high-maintenance features is the only rational way to ensure the park's longevity.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"It's refreshing to see everyone finally aligning with reality. Let's just ensure ""simple"" doesn't mean ""ignoring the tram commuters."" If we don't pave where people actually walk, they'll just create a new swamp.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
51,2,4,pass,Shunichi,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
52,3,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
53,3,,status,Minato,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
54,3,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
55,3,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Victoria,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
57,3,1,talk,Minato,,"I think Candidate C, the Sports Terraces, might be the safest. It's on the southern side, which I found is easier to fence off, and it doesn't seem to need as much big digging in the center.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,May,,"I have to disagree, Minato. Candidate C might be easy to fence, but look at B. A paved plaza is a dream for the budget! Hard surfaces are way cheaper to maintain than lawns or courts.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"I worry about Candidate A and D. My research showed that our young trees suffered without proper watering, and a wetland could become a burden if the care is forgotten. A modest plaza seems more enduring.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"I must agree with Shizue. Candidates A and D require intensive, specialized care that our seven remaining staff members simply cannot provide. A paved plaza is the only option that doesn't risk operational collapse.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Candidate B is the only one that doesn't fight the site. It acknowledges the need for hard surfaces where people actually walk and avoids the drainage nightmare of a wetland or the watering failures of a woodland.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@May, @Shunichi, if the plaza is in the center, will it be hard to fence off? I'm worried that if we dig there, the clay and slippage might make the work take a long time.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""May"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,May,,"@Minato, a little bit of digging now is worth a thousand headaches later! I'd rather deal with some clay during construction than a permanent budget leak for the next decade. B is just too efficient to pass up.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Minato, it is natural to be concerned about the work, but perhaps a paved space is the kindest choice for everyone. It will not wither like the trees did, and it gives our tired staff a chance to breathe.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Minato, while the construction phase may be challenging, the operational phase is where the real risk lies. A plaza requires far less daily intervention than the other options, making it the most sustainable choice for our depleted rota.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Minato, the clay is a construction hurdle, not a permanent failure. I'd rather have a few grumpy contractors now than a permanent mud pit in the center. B is the only rational choice here.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Minato,,"I understand. If everyone thinks the plaza is the best way to help the staff and the budget, then I want to agree too. I just hope the workers are careful with the clay!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,May,,Now we're talking! It's wonderful to see us all on the same page. Let's go with the Market Plaza; it's the only choice that doesn't treat the city's wallet like an open buffet.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Shizue,,It is a relief to see us in such harmony. A plaza is a gentle solution that respects our limits and ensures the park remains a welcoming place for years to come. I am happy to support Candidate B.,"{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Victoria,,I am also satisfied. Candidate B minimizes the burden on our limited personnel and avoids the high-maintenance pitfalls of the other plans. It is the most responsible choice for the city's long-term management.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,It's almost a miracle we've reached a consensus this quickly. Candidate B is the only plan that doesn't ignore the laws of physics or the reality of our payroll. I'm voting for the Market Plaza.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,4,talk,Minato,,I will vote for Candidate B. It makes me happy that we all agree on a plan that helps the staff and the budget. I hope the plaza becomes a lovely place for everyone!,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,4,talk,May,,I'm voting for Candidate B! It's the only plan that doesn't treat the city's wallet like an open buffet. Let's get that plaza built and keep our budget in the black!,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,4,talk,Shizue,,I shall also cast my vote for Candidate B. It is a sensible and lasting choice that will not break the hearts of our staff or the city's budget.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Victoria,,I vote for Candidate B. It is the only option that ensures the park remains functional and well-kept despite our severe staffing shortages. It is the most rational and sustainable path forward.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,I'm voting for Candidate B. It's the only option that doesn't pretend the park is a postcard. Let's build the plaza and stop fighting the mud.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
